{"data":{"slug":"can-machine-learning-beat-elo","title":"Can Machine Learning Beat Elo in Professional League of Legends?","research_question":"Does a logistic regression with pre-game features predict single-game outcomes better than an Elo benchmark, in terms of probability accuracy (Brier score, log loss) on a later, untouched test period?","motivation":"Elo is simple, transparent and hard to beat in many sports. If extra features do not improve out-of-sample probability accuracy, the added complexity is not justified. Separating a calibrated Elo from a feature-rich model shows whether any gain comes from calibration (including the blue-side effect) or from new information.","methodology":["Unit: one game. Target: blue side wins (1/0).","Elo: initial 1500, expected score 1/(1+10^((Rb-Ra)/400)), updated after every game in time order. K-factor (8-80) and between-season shrinkage (0-0.75) chosen by validation log loss.","League offsets: a team's rating is its league's level plus a team component. Games between leagues also move the two league levels (step k_league, 0-32, chosen on validation; 0 = flat Elo). New teams start at their league's level. The 'Elo baseline' below is the selected version; flat Elo is reported separately.","Calibrated Elo: logistic regression on the Elo difference only; its intercept estimates the blue-side advantage.","Logistic regression: six pre-specified pre-game features (Elo difference, recent and historical shrunk win rates, recent opponent strength, experience, Elo difference x international event). Standardised inside the pipeline, fitted on training data only; L2 strength chosen on validation.","Chronological split 70/15/15 by date after a 90-day burn-in; games where either team has fewer than 5 earlier games are excluded from all models alike. Final logistic models are refit on train+validation and scored once on the test period.","Every feature uses games with an earlier timestamp only. Post-game statistics are never used.","Comparison: paired cluster bootstrap (2,000 resamples) of the per-game loss difference on identical test games, resampling whole series (approximated as same tournament, same two teams, same UTC day)."],"limitations":["Series are approximated from the data (no series id in the source); two series between the same teams on the same day would be merged, which makes intervals slightly more conservative.","All teams start at the same rating, and regions are linked only by international events, so cross-region rating levels are uncertain.","Roster changes, patches and drafts are not modelled.","Results describe this sample period and these leagues; they may not transfer to other periods."],"references":["Elo, A. E. (1978). The Rating of Chessplayers, Past and Present. Arco Publishing.","Brier, G. W. (1950). Verification of forecasts expressed in terms of probability. Monthly Weather Review, 78(1), 1-3.","Hvattum, L. M., & Arntzen, H. (2010). Using ELO ratings for match result prediction in association football. International Journal of Forecasting, 26(3), 460-470.","Niculescu-Mizil, A., & Caruana, R. (2005). Predicting good probabilities with supervised learning. Proceedings of the 22nd International Conference on Machine Learning, 625-632.","Efron, B., & Tibshirani, R. J. (1993). An Introduction to the Bootstrap. Chapman & Hall.","Sevenhuysen, T. Oracle's Elixir: LoL esports match data. https://oracleselixir.com/tools/downloads"],"conclusion_rule":"Conclusions are generated from the bootstrap intervals: a model is called better only if the 95% interval of its Brier difference excludes zero.","status":"completed","status_note":null,"data":{"source":"Oracle's Elixir professional League of Legends match data (yearly CSV files).","files":[{"filename":"2020_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"4c271d944d37","coverage_start":"2020-01-03T07:33:26Z","coverage_end":"2020-12-27T11:06:48Z","rows_accepted":116880},{"filename":"2021_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"bf1b54172f7d","coverage_start":"2021-01-02T07:40:39Z","coverage_end":"2021-12-26T13:22:45Z","rows_accepted":147490},{"filename":"2022_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"76b7cb8afc1c","coverage_start":"2022-01-10T07:44:08Z","coverage_end":"2022-12-27T12:43:43Z","rows_accepted":150228},{"filename":"2023_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"efe4d2abe53e","coverage_start":"2023-01-10T17:07:16Z","coverage_end":"2023-12-31T11:48:06Z","rows_accepted":133142},{"filename":"2024_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"a2c67680a53c","coverage_start":"2024-01-01T05:13:15Z","coverage_end":"2024-12-08T09:03:13Z","rows_accepted":122436},{"filename":"2025_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"882245414e94","coverage_start":"2025-01-11T11:11:24Z","coverage_end":"2025-12-29T10:52:27Z","rows_accepted":120528},{"filename":"2026_LoL_esports_match_data_from_OraclesElixir.csv","sha256":"5bbfb43fd934","coverage_start":"2026-01-01T09:14:49Z","coverage_end":"2026-11-17T19:42:11Z","rows_accepted":119232}]},"sample_period":{"train":{"n":47070,"start":"2020-04-02 07:47:17+00:00","end":"2024-08-11 07:11:20+00:00","blue_win_rate":0.5269810919906522},"validation":{"n":10086,"start":"2024-08-11 08:17:21+00:00","end":"2025-09-23 17:11:40+00:00","blue_win_rate":0.53410668253024},"test":{"n":10087,"start":"2025-09-23 17:28:10+00:00","end":"2026-11-14 23:18:11+00:00","blue_win_rate":0.5350451075641915},"train_end":"2024-08-11 07:37:44.400000+00:00","validation_end":"2025-09-23 17:23:13+00:00","burn_in_end":"2020-04-02 07:33:26+00:00","data_start":"2020-01-03 07:33:26+00:00","data_end":"2026-11-17 19:42:11+00:00"},"results":{"model_table":[{"model":"Constant 50% (coin flip)","model_key":"baseline_50","n":10087,"accuracy":0.5350451075641915,"precision":0.5350451075641915,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.6971066907775768,"ece":0.03504510756419155,"roc_auc":null,"brier":0.25,"log_loss":0.6931471805599453,"base_rate_blue