strap interval includes zero.","Logistic regression vs calibrated Elo: brier difference -0.00062 (95% CI -0.00104 to -0.00023); lower (better) than calibrated Elo, and the 95% bootstrap interval excludes zero.","Size of the gain: the logistic regression lowers the Elo Brier score by 0.54%. Accuracy moves from 64.7% (Elo) to 64.9%.","Confidence intervals: series (cluster bootstrap), 4584 resampling units.","League offsets (k_league = 16) vs flat Elo: Brier 0.2176 vs 0.2230, difference -0.00543 (95% CI -0.00675 to -0.00406), lower (better); a 2.43% change.","On the 3095 test games between teams from different leagues, the Brier difference is -0.01539 (95% CI -0.01952 to -0.01117).","Prevalence baseline (always predict the earlier blue-side win rate): Brier 0.2488, accuracy 53.5%. Elo improves on it by 0.0312 Brier points.","Sensitivity: clustering by tournament (126 tournaments) instead of series gives a logistic vs calibrated Elo interval of -0.00106 to -0.00017.","Tree models (validation only): No tree model beats logistic regression on validation, so none is deployed or scored on the test period.","Estimated blue-side effect: with equal Elo, the calibrated model gives blue 53.2%."],"interpretation":"Statistically, the pre-game features add predictive information beyond a calibrated Elo in this test period (the interval excludes zero). Practically, the gain is small: 0.00062 Brier points, about 0.29% of the calibrated Elo score, and accuracy barely moves. Elo already carries most of the signal. A structural change to the benchmark (league offsets) improves accuracy more than the machine-learning features do on top of it: modelling how leagues relate matters more than adding predictors."},"meta":{"game":"lol","data_status":"available","data_type":"historical","source":"Oracle's Elixir","attribution":"Data: Oracle's Elixir (oracleselixir.com), Tim Sevenhuysen. Game statistics © Riot Games.","sample_period":{"start":"2020-01-03T07:33:26Z","end":"2026-11-17T19:42:11Z"},